        code: { lang: 'math', src: 'h-parameters (common emitter):\n  hie = input impedance = beta * re\n  hre = reverse voltage ratio, usually negligible\n  hfe = forward current gain = beta\n  hoe = output admittance = 1/ro\n\nHybrid pi (high frequency):\n  gm   = IC / 26 mV        transconductance\n  rpi  = beta / gm = beta * re\n  ro   = VA / IC\n  C_pi, C_mu: the capacitances that set the bandwidth\n\nCheck:  gm * rpi = beta' },
        mistake: 'Students use h-parameter values from a datasheet without checking the bias conditions at which they were measured. Every h-parameter varies with collector current, and a value quoted at 1 mA can be substantially wrong at 10 mA.',
