        definition:
          'The gain expression contains the total AC load at the collector, which is the collector resistor in parallel with whatever the stage is driving. Connecting a load therefore always reduces the gain, and the reduction is severe when the load is comparable with or smaller than RC. The no-load or unloaded gain quoted in a datasheet or a first calculation is an upper bound that is never achieved in use. For cascaded stages the load on one stage is the input impedance of the next, which is why the gain of a chain is always less than the product of the individual unloaded gains.',
