        definition:
          'Once the internal details are settled, an amplifier stage is completely described at its terminals by three numbers: the input impedance Zi, the output impedance Zo, and the no-load voltage gain Avnl. Any stage can then be replaced by that model, and a chain of stages analysed by repeated application of dividers at each junction. The systems view separates the device-level work of Module 2 from the interconnection work here, and it is the same abstraction used throughout engineering: characterise the block, then compose the blocks.',
