        definition:
          'Feedback returns part of the output to the input, where it is combined with the applied signal. Two choices define any feedback arrangement: what is sampled at the output, voltage or current, and how it is mixed at the input, in series or in shunt. When the returned signal opposes the input the feedback is negative and the amplifier operates on the difference, called the error signal. The loop gain, the product of the forward gain and the feedback fraction, is the single number that determines how much every property improves, and the whole subject is the consequences of making that product large.',
