        definition:
          'Combining the two sampling choices with the two mixing choices gives four topologies, each with a characteristic effect on the terminal impedances. Voltage-series feedback samples the output voltage and mixes in series, raising the input impedance and lowering the output impedance — the arrangement of a non-inverting operational amplifier and of an emitter follower. Voltage-shunt lowers both. Current-series raises both. Current-shunt lowers the input and raises the output. The rule is mechanical: series mixing raises input impedance, shunt mixing lowers it, voltage sampling lowers output impedance, current sampling raises it.',
