        definition:
          'The FET gain parameter is transconductance, the rate of change of drain current with gate-source voltage, which is the slope of the transfer characteristic at the operating point. Differentiating the square law gives gm equal to 2 IDSS over the magnitude of VP times one minus VGS over VP, so gm is largest at zero gate bias and falls to zero at pinch-off. The small-signal model is correspondingly simple: an open circuit at the gate, reflecting the absence of gate current, and a voltage-controlled current source of gm times the gate-source voltage at the drain, with an output resistance in parallel.',
